### Rust: Boolean Flags (Switches) in Clap Derive

Source: https://docs.rs/clap/latest/src/clap/_derive/_tutorial.rs.html?search=std%3A%3Avec

Shows how to implement boolean flags (switches) that toggle behavior using `bool` fields. Also demonstrates counting flag occurrences with the Count action.

```rust
#[derive(Parser)]
struct Cli {
    /// Enable verbose output
    #[arg(short, long)]
    verbose: bool,
}

fn main() {
    let cli = Cli::parse();

    if cli.verbose {
        println!("Verbose mode enabled.");
    }
}
```

```rust
#[derive(Parser)]
struct Cli {
    /// Increase log level
    #[arg(short, long, action = clap::ArgAction::Count)]
    v: u8,
}

fn main() {
    let cli = Cli::parse();

    match cli.v {
        0 => println!("Log level: INFO"),
        1 => println!("Log level: DEBUG"),
        _ => println!("Log level: TRACE"),
    }
}
```

